e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329721 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "55d7cd50-6834-55b6-a52f-4f6d251b49dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329721 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528147 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528218 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528147 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528147 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f8/f8a71c2cbb351253304bca516db5b4b7ca7ed745264083f9eb2bbdb918e19cc0.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "129248be-068c-5fed-a900-5e4f8d0a77cb" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528147 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528147 #edb/ref 1074 "The angles of a triangle sum to $180^{\\circ}$. Thus the included angle is\n\n$$\nm∠B=180^{\\circ}-73^{\\circ}-73^{\\circ}=34^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=9.28, \\\\ a & =BC=9.28, \\\\ m∠B & ={34}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{34}^{∘}=0.559\\,193,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9.28\\cdot 9.28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{34}^{∘} \\\\  & =43.0592\\cdot (0.559\\,193) \\\\  & ≈24.08,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528157 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528160 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528157 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528157 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/45/4507bd5611cdf0324c470755c19274b04b9572b9c416e57b319aa444fce41e8b.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528157 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3b677441-8745-5947-a9e5-2dd19f60b63a" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528157 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528157 #edb/ref 1074 "The angles of a triangle sum to $180^{\\circ}$. Thus the included angle is\n\n$$\nm∠B=180^{\\circ}-46^{\\circ}-46^{\\circ}=88^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=27.26, \\\\ a & =BC=27.26, \\\\ m∠B & ={88}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{88}^{∘}=0.999\\,391,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 27.26\\cdot 27.26\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{88}^{∘} \\\\  & =371.5538\\cdot (0.999\\,391) \\\\  & ≈371.33,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528162 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528219 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528162 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528162 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b4/b4d346c76ff55f7e183aefa579c49b54022e75ea4b723c5d74954c5257dcdf2f.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{ft}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186528162 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4cab