 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186546279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546931 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cc7013e3-dd6c-5307-aa48-3cf975733d4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547012 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547012 #edb/ref 1069 "q-54340" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547012 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547012 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/87/873c7f6b6e036f592f693bf2d20e1980b890f888d08af40b775cb77deba07a76.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the parallelogram $ABCD?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547012 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66cc8550-5653-59d7-83fc-1ba0962c771f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547012 #edb/ref 1074 "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{BD}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ABD$ (see the illustration).\n\n![](images/75/7572dac85d8e6029b52d199bdfcb87b4a92ffafc008fe999c10848153f9f67d8.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ABD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{38}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{38}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈18.470,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ABD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 18.470 \\\\  & =36.940.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $37.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547025 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547025 #edb/ref 1069 "q-54338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547025 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547025 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/24/243e5fd1911db6fc7dc940a16082c7369c63f913d78d9e18324d977540a310cb.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547025 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81669d7f-c6da-5c9d-8581-df25b358ada6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547025 #edb/ref 1074 "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{BD}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△CBD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/da/da5c25d9e1e54a79b8e2c8532d4571dd42ccd4e6e6a3fa69aa1fc9075c19b39d.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△CBD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{CBD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(21)(12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & =126\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈115.107,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{CBD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 115.107 \\\\  & =230.214.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $230.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547048 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547048 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67680" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547048 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547048 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/a8/a8cd5ca7760d21ac5bd86cfb90486ccde755f4aba831808889a20e1ad467eaf9.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547048 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb68b570-72f8-5730-8942-1936207e20f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547048 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ab\\operatorname{sin}⁡C,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠C$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =CA=8, \\\\ a & =CB=10, \\\\ m∠A & ={43}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}=0.681\\,998,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =40\\cdot (0.681\\,998) \\\\  & ≈27.28\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547053 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547053 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547053 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547053 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/9b/9b922282db5fce22af7df867b36545077f7d609dc83ef97abf46d5f9814cbc3c.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547053 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cade1253-bc92-5811-80c5-a30e8af6f3ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547053 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=36, \\\\ b & =AC=36, \\\\ m∠A & ={70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}=0.939\\,693,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 36\\cdot 36\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =648\\cdot (0.939\\,693) \\\\  & ≈609\\,{\\text{mi}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547072 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547072 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67795" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547072 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547072 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/16/160b47689a56ef98c0a0d6b2df6dcf838857ba840ce017ac0707366304f68f83.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $112\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△BCD=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547072 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed23a91b-121e-53d9-8168-fa3e48b78557" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547072 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24\\cdot 16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =192\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =157.277… \\\\  & ≈157\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =157-112 \\\\  & =45\\,{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547082 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547082 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67793" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547082 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547082 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ca/ca15b4523cd12bdfb4661624eba58387e15ebef6e228c1740b4582ba6af556a9.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $175{\\text{ in}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547082 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe2449e6-7778-52c7-8e7c-b90034a289a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547082 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 27\\cdot 30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{35}^{∘} \\\\  & =405\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{35}^{∘} \\\\  & =232.298… \\\\  & ≈232{\\text{ in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =232-175 \\\\  & =57\\,{\\text{ in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
